    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Welcome to the Void.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You are a low-level contractor working for Void Tech, a mega-corporation specializing in satellite repairs and orbital maintenance. Your job? Fix what's broken, dodge space debris, and keep your oxygen levels in check\u2014all while dealing with shady corporate policies and the occasional &quot;classified&quot; mission.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >But something is off. As you take on routine contracts for NASAS, WESA, ISROR, and private companies like SpaceG, strange things start happening. Systems fail without explanation, encrypted messages appear in your mission logs, and your only lifeline\u2014Mission Control\u2014seems to be hiding something.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Do you follow orders blindly, or dig deeper to uncover the truth?</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Key Features</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\ud83d\ude80 <strong>Hardcore but Accessible Space Simulation</strong> \u2013 Manage oxygen, thrusters, and tools while floating in zero gravity. No hand-holding\u2014just you, your EVA suit, and the cold void.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\ud83d\udef0\ufe0f <strong>Diverse Missions</strong> \u2013 Work with (or against) agencies like NASAS, WESA, and private space firms. Repair satellites, retrieve black-box data, and sometimes... cover things up.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\ud83d\udca5 <strong>Physics-Based Hazards</strong> \u2013 Watch out for orbital debris, solar storms, and unpredictable equipment failures. A single mistake can send you spinning into the void.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\ud83d\udd75\ufe0f <strong>Uncover a Deep Sci-Fi Mystery</strong> \u2013 Strange transmissions, missing satellites, and encrypted files hint at something bigger than just broken tech. Will you find the truth or look the other way?</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Void Tech isn\u2019t just a job\u2014it\u2019s survival in orbit.</strong> Are you ready to float into the unknown?</p>",
